Routing capture transport and level-pool initialization interoperate with
NOAA-OWP/t-route, pinned 12a8eae0cdfed437143c590659fa7077605a5e70.
Apache License, Version 2.0, January 2004; actual LICENSE read before porting,
retained in notices/t-route-LICENSE. No upstream NOTICE at this pin.
routing_capture.rs transports typed native inputs to resident CUDA payloads;
reservoir initialization comes from the reservoir owner's sealed Rust output.
The native capture importer is an explicit referee replay tool; it does not
claim independent reconstruction of the captured graph from a GeoPackage.
collapse.rs translates HYFeaturesNetwork.py waterbody preprocessing and
nhd_network.py replacement/reversal into Rust, with explicit insertion order
and rejection of ambiguous outlet/membership data. Case-specific numeric ID
repairs from upstream are not embedded in this generic implementation.

Optional source-archive acquisition binary uses the published libarchive C API.
System libarchive 3.8.5 (Ubuntu 3.8.5-1ubuntu2.3) notices were read before use:
"Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
modification, are permitted" (BSD-2-Clause for the library, with file-specific
permissive notices retained in notices/libarchive-system-COPYRIGHT).
No libarchive source is translated. The production bridge and normal CLI do
not link libarchive; only --features source-archive enables the separate tool.

dbf.rs implements the fixed-width interchange format independently from its
public format descriptions; no vendor program code is copied:
https://www.dbase.com/Knowledgebase/INT/db7_file_fmt.htm (format background)
https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000325.shtml
Only dBASE III no-memo tables are accepted; gauge character IDs stay strings.

source_geometry.rs independently implements the published SHP/SHX file layout:
ESRI Shapefile Technical Description, July 1998,
https://www.esri.com/content/dam/esrisites/sitecore-archive/Files/Pdfs/library/whitepapers/pdfs/shapefile.pdf
The specification was consulted, not copied or redistributed. No ESRI or GDAL
program source is translated. Original EPA/USGS NHDPlus data attribution and
provider metadata/member inventory are retained separately from software terms.

Optional source-netcdf acquisition binary calls the published NetCDF-C API.
System NetCDF-C 4.9.3 (Ubuntu 1:4.9.3-1build2) copyright was read before use:
BSD-3-Clause, "Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
modification, are permitted". File-specific permissive NetCDF grants and the
complete system copyright are retained in notices/netcdf-system-COPYRIGHT.
No NetCDF implementation is copied. Only rw_hydrofabric_netcdf_subset links
NetCDF-C/HDF5; the production raw bridge remains independent of both libraries.
Dataset terms must be reviewed independently; NOAA hosting alone does not settle
explicitly attributed third-party inputs. This tool performs stored-value
transport only, with no physical defaults, unit conversion or crosswalk policy.
